# Curated requirement phrases for requirement-content traceability.
#
# One line per requirement ID: ID|phrase|phrase|...
# Each phrase MUST be verbatim (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed)
# wording from that requirement's own text in REQUIREMENTS.md; the verifier
# hard-fails on any phrase that is not, so a phrase can never silently
# satisfy a different requirement. A spec claiming an ID passes only when
# at least one of its phrases appears in the spec body.
#
# Coverage is enforced: every requirement ID in REQUIREMENTS.md must have an
# entry here (the extension's bash suite checks it), and every phrase is
# validated against REQUIREMENTS.md on every run. A claim with no curated
# phrase fails closed as a maintainer action.
#
# This file is your starting point: replace the sample entries below with
# phrases from your own REQUIREMENTS.md. Pick distinctive wording - not
# IDs or headings - that a spec must carry for the claim to be true.
#
# Sample (matches examples/ in the template):
# GREET-1|greet each person by name|personal greeting
# LANG-1|language parameter|default language
# OUT-1|greeting log with redacted recipient data
